# HONOR MagicBook Pro 14 2025 (FMB-P): inhibit the FocalTech FTSC1000 touchscreen's
# bogus SECOND HID collection ("FTSC1000:00 2808:5662 UNKNOWN"), which spams
# KEY_MICMUTE (~30/s) while the panel is touched — toggling the microphone and
# confusing Fn+F7. Inhibiting it leaves only the real multitouch device in use.
# (Touchscreen *power* comes from the DSDT PowerResource fix, not this rule.)
# Source: colorcube/Linux-on-Honor-Magicbook-14-Pro #20 / stretch/touchscreen.md
SUBSYSTEM=="input", ATTRS{name}=="FTSC1000:00 2808:5662 UNKNOWN", RUN+="/bin/sh -c 'echo 1 > /sys$env{DEVPATH}/../inhibited'"
